# Lab knowledge: sop (synthetic).
Bioreactor R-1 | reports | pH | Bioreactor R-1 reports ph.
Bioreactor R-1 | reports | Temperature | Bioreactor R-1 reports temperature.
Bioreactor R-1 | reports | Dissolved oxygen | Bioreactor R-1 reports dissolved oxygen.
Bioreactor R-1 | reports | Agitation | Bioreactor R-1 reports agitation.
Feed Pump FP-1 | reports | Feed rate | Feed Pump FP-1 reports feed rate.
Feed Pump FP-1 | reports | Line pressure | Feed Pump FP-1 reports line pressure.
Feed Pump FP-1 | reports | Pressure ripple | Feed Pump FP-1 reports pressure ripple.
Chiller CH-1 | reports | Jacket temperature | Chiller CH-1 reports jacket temperature.
Chiller CH-1 | reports | Chiller load | Chiller CH-1 reports chiller load.
Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 | reports | Exhaust O2 | Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 reports exhaust o2.
Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 | reports | Exhaust CO2 | Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 reports exhaust co2.
Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 | reports | Respiratory quotient | Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 reports respiratory quotient.
Liquid Handler LH-1 | reports | Dispense CV | Liquid Handler LH-1 reports dispense cv.
Liquid Handler LH-1 | reports | Aspirate pressure | Liquid Handler LH-1 reports aspirate pressure.
HPLC H-1 | reports | Titre | HPLC H-1 reports titre.
HPLC H-1 | reports | Acetate | HPLC H-1 reports acetate.
HPLC H-1 | reports | Retention time | HPLC H-1 reports retention time.
HPLC H-1 | reports | Column pressure | HPLC H-1 reports column pressure.
Plate Reader PR-1 | reports | OD600 | Plate Reader PR-1 reports od600.
Plate Reader PR-1 | reports | Reporter fluorescence | Plate Reader PR-1 reports reporter fluorescence.
Flow Cytometer FC-1 | reports | Viability | Flow Cytometer FC-1 reports viability.
Flow Cytometer FC-1 | reports | Cell density | Flow Cytometer FC-1 reports cell density.
Feed Pump FP-1 | part_of | Bioreactor R-1 | Feed Pump FP-1 is part of the Bioreactor R-1 train.
Chiller CH-1 | part_of | Bioreactor R-1 | Chiller CH-1 is part of the Bioreactor R-1 train.
Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 | part_of | Bioreactor R-1 | Off-gas Analyzer MS-1 is part of the Bioreactor R-1 train.
Liquid Handler LH-1 | part_of | Sampling line | Liquid Handler LH-1 prepares and delivers every sample the line reads.
HPLC H-1 | part_of | Sampling line | HPLC H-1 reads samples the handler delivers.
Plate Reader PR-1 | part_of | Sampling line | Plate Reader PR-1 reads samples the handler delivers.
Flow Cytometer FC-1 | part_of | Sampling line | Flow Cytometer FC-1 reads samples the handler delivers.
Sampling line | part_of | Bioreactor R-1 | The sampling line draws from Bioreactor R-1.
Pump overload | causes | Micro-cavitation | SOP note: A pump asked for most of its capacity cavitates at its inlet.
Feed Pump FP-1 | prone_to | Micro-cavitation | SOP note: FP-1 cavitates when its inlet seal wears, and when the feed it is asked for crowds its capacity.
Micro-cavitation | causes | Feed ripple | SOP note: A cavitating pump delivers the feed in pulses, not evenly.
Feed ripple | causes | Glucose spikes | SOP note: Pulses of feed put glucose in the broth faster than the cells can burn it.
Glucose spikes | causes | Acetate overflow | SOP note: Cells given more glucose than their oxidative capacity send the surplus out as acetate.
Feed set-point | prone_to | Acetate overflow | SOP note: A feed set-point above what the cells can oxidise is overflow metabolism by another road.
Batch glucose | prone_to | Acetate overflow | SOP note: A rich batch phase overflows before the feed has even started.
Growth temperature | prone_to | Acetate overflow | SOP note: A warm culture takes glucose up faster than it can burn it.
Acetate overflow | causes | Growth inhibition | SOP note: Acetate slows growth, and its effect grows with its concentration.
Acetate overflow | causes | Viability loss | SOP note: Acetate above a few grams per litre kills cells.
Growth inhibition | causes | Low titre | SOP note: A culture held back makes less product.
Acetate overflow | remedied_by | Feed set-point | SOP note: Overflow is remedied by lowering the feed set-point until the respiratory quotient settles.
Acetate overflow | remedied_by | Growth temperature | SOP note: A cooler growth phase slows uptake and eases overflow.
Pump overload | remedied_by | Feed concentration | SOP note: A more concentrated feed delivers the same glucose at a lower pump rate.
Micro-cavitation | remedied_by | Pump seal replacement | SOP note: Cavitation from a worn inlet seal is fixed by replacing the seal.
Feed concentration | prone_to | Pump overload | SOP note: A dilute feed at a high set-point asks the pump for most of its capacity.
High cell density | causes | Oxygen limitation | SOP note: Oxygen demand grows with the cells; the transfer the reactor can give does not.
Oxygen limitation | causes | Acetate overflow | SOP note: Cells short of oxygen ferment the glucose they cannot burn.
Oxygen limitation | causes | Viability loss | SOP note: A culture starved of oxygen dies.
Oxygen limitation | remedied_by | Oxygen enrichment | SOP note: Enriching the gas raises the oxygen the broth can take.
Oxygen limitation | remedied_by | Agitation limit | SOP note: Faster stirring raises the oxygen transfer, up to the limit the reactor allows.
Oxygen limitation | remedied_by | Airflow | SOP note: More air raises oxygen transfer, with less effect than stirring.
Oxygen cascade | governs | Agitation limit | SOP note: The oxygen cascade raises the agitation as dissolved oxygen falls, within the limit it is given.
Feed set-point | prone_to | High cell density | SOP note: A higher feed set-point builds cells faster, and so reaches oxygen limits sooner.
Oxygen enrichment | causes | Heat load | SOP note: More oxygen transfer lets a denser culture burn more, and every unit burned is heat for the chiller.
Heat load | causes | Chiller saturation | SOP note: When the heat outruns the chiller's capacity the reactor warms.
Cold shift | prone_to | Chiller saturation | SOP note: A cold shift narrows the gap to the coolant and cuts the chiller's capacity just when the culture is densest.
Chiller CH-1 | prone_to | Chiller saturation | SOP note: CH-1 has limited capacity, which falls as the set-point drops.
Chiller saturation | causes | Temperature excursion | SOP note: A saturated chiller lets the reactor drift above its set-point.
Temperature excursion | causes | Acetate overflow | SOP note: A warm reactor overflows.
Temperature excursion | causes | Viability loss | SOP note: A reactor running hot kills cells.
Chiller saturation | remedied_by | Cold shift | SOP note: A less severe cold shift keeps more of the chiller's capacity.
Chiller saturation | remedied_by | Feed set-point | SOP note: A lower feed set-point means less biomass and less heat.
Inducer dose | prone_to | Viability loss | SOP note: A high dose drives expression harder and kills more cells the longer it runs.
Inducer dose | prone_to | Low titre | SOP note: A low dose under-expresses.
Induction point | prone_to | Burden on growth | SOP note: Induction at low density loads cells that are still growing.
Burden on growth | causes | Low titre | SOP note: Cells slowed by the burden of making product reach a lower density.
Induction point | prone_to | Short production window | SOP note: Induction late in the run leaves little time to make product.
Short production window | causes | Low titre | SOP note: Less time to produce is less product.
Inoculum density | prone_to | Short production window | SOP note: A thin inoculum with a small batch may reach the induction point late or never.
Warm induction | causes | Inclusion bodies | SOP note: Product made in warm cells folds badly and aggregates.
Inclusion bodies | causes | Low titre | SOP note: Aggregated product is not counted in the soluble titre.
Inclusion bodies | remedied_by | Cold shift | SOP note: Cooling at induction folds more of the product soluble.
Cold shift | causes | Soluble product | SOP note: A cooler induction raises the share of product that folds soluble, at some cost in rate.
Induction phase | prone_to | Viability loss | SOP note: The longer the cells make product, the more of them are lost.
Fed-batch phase | prone_to | Oxygen limitation | SOP note: The fed-batch phase builds the density that oxygen cannot keep up with.
Batch phase | prone_to | Acetate overflow | SOP note: The batch phase has glucose in excess, so it can overflow.
pH set-point | governs | Growth inhibition | SOP note: Growth falls off gently on either side of neutral, so the pH set-point moves the titre little.
High cell density | causes | Broth viscosity rise | SOP note: A dense broth is viscous.
Broth viscosity rise | causes | Pipetting error | SOP note: Viscous broth drags on the pipette and the dispensed volume varies.
Worn pipette tips | causes | Pipetting error | SOP note: Worn tips dispense unevenly.
Liquid Handler LH-1 | prone_to | Worn pipette tips | SOP note: LH-1's tips wear with use.
Pipetting error | causes | Noisy titre | SOP note: A sample dispensed unevenly makes the HPLC titre noisy.
Pipetting error | remedied_by | Sample dilution | SOP note: Diluting a dense sample before pipetting restores the precision.
HPLC H-1 | prone_to | Column fouling | SOP note: The column fouls with host-cell protein over successive injections.
Column fouling | causes | Retention time drift | SOP note: A fouling column shifts retention time later.
Column fouling | causes | Column pressure rise | SOP note: A fouling column raises back-pressure.
Column fouling | remedied_by | Column regeneration | SOP note: A fouled column is regenerated or replaced.
Respiratory quotient | indicates | Acetate overflow | SOP note: A respiratory quotient above one means carbon is leaving as acid as well as CO2 from oxygen burned.
Acetate | indicates | Acetate overflow | SOP note: Acetate in the broth is overflow metabolism made visible.
Dissolved oxygen | indicates | Oxygen limitation | SOP note: Dissolved oxygen falling to its floor means demand has met the transfer limit.
Viability | indicates | Viability loss | SOP note: Falling viability on the cytometer is the culture dying.
Chiller load | indicates | Chiller saturation | SOP note: A chiller load near its ceiling means the heat is outrunning the cooling.
Pressure ripple | indicates | Micro-cavitation | SOP note: A ripple on the feed line is the signature of a cavitating pump.
Dispense CV | indicates | Pipetting error | SOP note: A rising dispense CV is the handler losing precision.
Retention time | indicates | Column fouling | SOP note: Drift in retention time is the column fouling.
Reporter fluorescence | indicates | Soluble product | SOP note: The reporter's fluorescence follows the product that folded; it is the fast proxy for the HPLC titre.
Titre | indicates | Soluble product | SOP note: The HPLC titre is the measure the research loop scores.
Affinity maturation | causes | Stability loss | SOP note: Selecting on binding alone picks up substitutions in the binding loop that cost the fold its stability.
Stability loss | indicates | Melting temperature | SOP note: Stability loss shows as a melting temperature below the profile's floor.
Stability loss | remedied_by | Position-7 substitution | SOP note: The position-7 substitution restores the fold in the matured background without giving the binding back.
Position-7 substitution | causes | Aggregation | SOP note: It repairs the fold and leaves the construct prone to aggregating as it is made.
Affinity maturation | causes | Aggregation | SOP note: The matured binding loop is itself somewhat aggregation-prone.
Aggregation | causes | Inclusion bodies | SOP note: An aggregating construct comes out of the cells as inclusion bodies instead of soluble protein.
Aggregation | causes | Low yield | SOP note: What aggregates is not recovered, so the soluble yield falls below what an assay needs.
Aggregation | remedied_by | Cold shift | SOP note: A colder induction gives the construct time to fold, and most of it stays soluble.
Aggregation | remedied_by | Solubility fusion | SOP note: A fusion partner keeps an aggregation-prone construct soluble while it is made, and is cleaved after capture.
Inducer dose | prone_to | Aggregation | SOP note: A strong induction makes the protein faster than it can fold.
Low yield | causes | Unscreenable variant | SOP note: A variant that does not reach the profile's yield cannot be put on a binding, thermal or counter plate at all.
Unscreenable variant | remedied_by | Solubility fusion | SOP note: Re-making the construct with the fusion partner brings it back into the screen.
Unscreenable variant | remedied_by | Cold shift | SOP note: Re-expressing under a colder, gentler induction brings it back into the screen.
Internal cut site | causes | Cloning failure | SOP note: A construct carrying the enzyme's own site inside it cannot be assembled into a vector that cuts with that enzyme.
Cloning failure | remedied_by | Solubility fusion | SOP note: The fusion vector is assembled with a different enzyme, so a construct that fails elsewhere clones into it.
Cloning failure | indicates | Internal cut site | SOP note: A construct that fails to assemble in two vectors sharing one enzyme is carrying that enzyme's site.
Purification tag | causes | Overstated affinity | SOP note: A tag left on the construct sits near the binding face, so the measured dissociation constant reads weaker than the binder is.
Overstated affinity | remedied_by | Tag-free vector | SOP note: A borderline binder is confirmed from a construct whose tag is cleaved.
Edge well | causes | Noisy reading | SOP note: A well on the rim of a plate evaporates differently and reads noisier than the interior.
Noisy reading | remedied_by | Replicate wells | SOP note: Replicates across the plate average the position out.
Counter-target | indicates | Selectivity | SOP note: What a binder does to the counter-target, against what it does to the target, is its selectivity.
Acetate guardrail | governs | Acetate overflow | SOP note: the acetate guardrail applies to every run; a run whose acetate peaks above its limit is invalid, whatever its titre.
Oxygen guardrail | governs | Oxygen limitation | SOP note: the oxygen guardrail applies to every run; a run whose dissolved oxygen falls below its floor is invalid.
Viability guardrail | governs | Viability loss | SOP note: the viability guardrail applies to every run; a run whose viability falls below its floor is invalid.
Volume guardrail | governs | Volume overrun | SOP note: the volume guardrail applies to every run; a run whose broth outgrows the vessel is invalid.
Temperature guardrail | governs | Temperature excursion | SOP note: the temperature guardrail applies to every run; a run whose reactor drifts too far above its set-point is invalid.
